      "text": "To find the value of \\( a \\) for which \\( g(a) = 0 \\) given the function \\( g(x) = 3x - 4 \\), we need to solve the equation:\n\n\\[ g(a) = 0 \\]\n\nSubstitute \\( g(x) \\) with \\( 3x - 4 \\):\n\n\\[ 3a - 4 = 0 \\]\n\nNow, solve for \\( a \\):\n\n1. Add 4 to both sides of the equation:\n\n\\[ 3a - 4 + 4 = 0 + 4 \\]\n\\[ 3a = 4 \\]\n\n2. Divide both sides by 3:\n\n\\[ a = \\frac{4}{3} \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( a \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}}\n\\]",
